expanded="true"
root="false"><fr:frontmatter><fr:anchor>482</fr:anchor><fr:taxon>Definition</fr:taxon><fr:addr>hejohns-000I</fr:addr><fr:route>hejohns-000I.xml</fr:route><fr:title>Subobject classifier</fr:title><fr:date><fr:year>2024</fr:year><fr:month>6</fr:month><fr:day>3</fr:day></fr:date><fr:date><fr:year>2024</fr:year><fr:month>6</fr:month><fr:day>4</fr:day></fr:date></fr:frontmatter><fr:mainmatter><fr:p>
    For a category <fr:tex>\mathcal {C}</fr:tex>, a <fr:em>subobject classifier</fr:em> is an object <fr:tex>Ω</fr:tex> together
    with a global element <fr:tex>true : 1 → Ω</fr:tex> such that <fr:tex>∀ A ∈  \mathcal {C} . ∀ s : S ↣ A. ∃!     χ_s : A → Ω.</fr:tex>
    <fr:embedded-tex
hash="e02927923b00b58796778a2184dd7584"><fr:embedded-tex-preamble>\usepackage {tikz-cd} \usepackage {unicode-math}</fr:embedded-tex-preamble><fr:embedded-tex-body>
         \begin {tikzcd}
            S  \ar [d, rightarrowtail, "s"'] \ar [r] \ar [dr, phantom, " \lrcorner ", very near start]  &amp; 1  \ar [d, rightarrowtail, "true"]  \\ 
            A  \ar [r, "χ_s"'] &amp; Ω
         \end {tikzcd}
    </fr:embedded-tex-body></fr:embedded-tex>
    is a pullback square.
</fr:p><fr:p>
    Notice that <fr:tex>true</fr:tex> is trivially monic since every <fr:link
href="hejohns-000K.xml"
type="local"
addr="hejohns-000K">global
    element</fr:link> is trivially monic. Recall that "monos are stable
    under pullback".
</fr:p><fr:p>
    This is from <fr:link
href="mclarty-1992.xml"
type="local"
addr="mclarty-1992">Elementary Categories, Elementary Toposes</fr:link>.
</fr:p></fr:mainmatter></fr:tree></fr:backlinks><fr:references><fr:tree
